      "The Regional Agricultural Cooperative of Campos Novos (Copercampos) operates in Santa Catarina, in the municipality known as the “Granary of Santa Catarina,” producing and marketing grains, seeds, agricultural inputs, and agro-industrial products. With a turnover of over R$4.2 billion, it is one of the largest cooperatives in the country. Copercampos is developing three strategic sustainability projects, reinforcing its commitment to the environment and its responsibility towards climate change.\n\nA number of situations led to this initiative. The first was the absence of calculations for the mitigation of Greenhouse Gas (GHG) emissions at the cooperative’s institutional events. Furthermore, in Copercampos' sustainability reports, the information on environmental practices was presented in a dispersed manner, without standardization and with low transparency. There were difficulties in measuring and communicating the organization's social, economic and environmental impacts. GHG emissions were also not measured and, as a result, there was a lack of knowledge about the cooperative's main sources of emissions.",
